.TH SOCKETPAIR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
socketpair \- create a connected socket pair
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int socketpair(int domain, int type, int protocol, int* descriptors);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes two connected descriptors to the supplied array. Linux typically uses
AF_UNIX and SOCK_STREAM or SOCK_DGRAM, with protocol zero.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR socket (3crunch),
.BR socketpair (2)
